window.LISTENING_DATA = [{"id":"2021-06-1","title":"2021年6月 第1套","audio":"listening/2021-06-1.ogg","duration":1382.84,"parts":[{"id":"2021-06-1-0","label":"新闻 1","questions":"第 1–2 题","start":41.87,"end":154.22,"sentences":[{"s":44.15,"e":55.29,"en":"And finally, in tonight's news, a nine-year-old boy named Joe, told not to draw in class, lands a job decorating a restaurant with his drawings.","zh":"最后，在今晚的新闻中，一位名叫乔的九岁男孩被告知不要在课堂上画画，但他却凭借自己的画作获得了一份为餐厅装饰的工作。"},{"s":55.29,"e":67.71,"en":"Rather than shutting down the habit of drawing in his school's workbook, Joe's parents decided to encourage his creativity by sending their son to an after-school art class.","zh":"Joe的父母没有阻止他在学校的练习册上画画的习惯，而是决定通过送儿子去上课外美术班来鼓励他的创造力。"},{"s":67.71,"e":76.07,"en":"His teacher recognized Joe's talent and posted all his work online, which led to something pretty wonderful.","zh":"他的老师发现了Joe的天赋，并将他的所有作品发布到网上，这引发了一些非常精彩的事情。"},{"s":76.07,"e":86.43,"en":"A restaurant named Number 4 in Newcastle contacted Joe's teacher to ask if the nine-year-old could come and decorate its dining room with his drawings.","zh":"纽卡斯尔一家名为Number 4的餐厅联系了乔的老师，询问这位9岁男孩是否可以来餐厅，用他的画作装饰餐厅。"},{"s":86.43,"e":94.49,"en":"Every day after school, Joe's dad drives him to the restaurant so he can put his ideas straight on the wall.","zh":"每天放学后，Joe的爸爸都会开车送他去餐厅，这样他就可以把自己的想法直接贴在墙上。"},{"s":94.49,"e":98.81,"en":"Once he's all done, the work will remain there permanently.","zh":"一旦他完成了所有工作，作品将永久保留在那里。"},{"s":98.81,"e":102.87,"en":"Joe's dad said, Joe is a really talented little boy.","zh":"Joe的爸爸说，Joe是个非常有天赋的小男孩。"},{"s":102.87,"e":154.22,"en":"He's excellent at school, he's great at football, but drawing is definitely what he is most passionate about.","zh":"他在学校表现出色，踢足球也很棒，但他最热衷的绝对是画画。"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-1","label":"新闻 2","questions":"第 3–4 题","start":154.22,"end":265.66,"sentences":[{"s":156.36,"e":167.78,"en":"Kirsteen Marshall, a 34-year-old mum of one, posted a tearful video on social media Wednesday, begging for the safe return of her beloved pet dog.","zh":"34岁的单亲妈妈Kirsteen Marshall周三在社交媒体上发布了一段泪流满面的视频，恳求她心爱的宠物狗平安归来。"},{"s":167.78,"e":177.96,"en":"After combing through the security video outside a Gaubles shop, Kirsteen has now posted an image of a man suspected of stealing the dog.","zh":"在仔细查看Gaubles商店外面的监控录像后，Kirsteen现在发布了一张涉嫌偷狗的男子的照片。"},{"s":177.96,"e":182.74,"en":"The image appears to show a man carrying the dog in his arms.","zh":"这张图片似乎显示一名男子抱着一只狗。"},{"s":182.74,"e":192.72,"en":"Kirsteen also believes the video obtained from the shop shows the dog being stolen by a man before driving off in a car which had been waiting nearby.","zh":"Kirsteen还认为，从商店获得的视频显示，一只狗被一名男子偷走，然后该男子驾车离开，车子一直在附近等候。"},{"s":192.72,"e":203.28,"en":"The family is now offering a £5,000 reward for the safe return of the dog after launching a social media campaign to find the thief.","zh":"这家人在社交媒体上发起了一场寻找小偷的活动，现在正悬赏5000英镑，以期爱犬平安归来。"},{"s":203.28,"e":209.22,"en":"The dog is six and a half years old and was last seen wearing a red collar.","zh":"这只狗六岁半，最后一次被人看见时戴着红色项圈。"},{"s":209.22,"e":217.2,"en":"Kirsteen said, we will pay that to anyone who brings him home as long as they are not responsible for his disappearance.","zh":"Kirsteen说，只要不是导致他失踪的人，我们就会向带他回家的人支付这笔钱。"},{"s":217.2,"e":265.66,"en":"Police are investigating the incident.","zh":"利比亚警方正在调查这一事件。"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-2","label":"新闻 3","questions":"第 5–7 题","start":265.66,"end":446.1,"sentences":[{"s":267.74,"e":278.48,"en":"London's Eggs and Bread Cafe offers boiled eggs, toast, jam, and bacon, as well as tea, coffee, and orange juice.","zh":"伦敦的Eggs and Bread咖啡馆供应水煮蛋、吐司、果酱和培根，以及茶、咖啡和橙汁。"},{"s":278.48,"e":283.42,"en":"But at the end of the meal, customers don't have to worry about the bill.","zh":"不过，在用餐结束时，顾客不必担心账单问题。"},{"s":283.42,"e":290.54,"en":"Hungry customers can pay whatever amount they can afford to eat at the cafe or nothing at all.","zh":"饥肠辘辘的顾客可以在咖啡馆用餐，支付自己负担得起的任何金额，也可以不支付任何费用。"},{"s":290.54,"e":297.0,"en":"Owner Guy Wilson says his cafe aims to build community rather than profits.","zh":"店主Guy Wilson表示，他的咖啡馆旨在建立社区，而不是追求利润。"},{"s":297.0,"e":307.62,"en":"He wants to provide a bridge for people to connect in an area that has been divided by class and wealth by providing affordable breakfasts.","zh":"他希望通过提供价格实惠的早餐，为人们搭建一座桥梁，让他们在一个被阶级和财富分割的地区建立联系。"},{"s":307.62,"e":316.18,"en":"The cafe is open in the mornings every day of the year and has two members of staff or supervisors on shift every day.","zh":"咖啡馆全年每天早上营业，每天都有两名员工或主管轮班。"},{"s":316.18,"e":323.34,"en":"The cafe doesn't use volunteers but pays its staff to ensure consistency in its service.","zh":"这家咖啡馆不使用志愿者，而是向员工支付薪酬，以确保服务的一致性。"},{"s":323.34,"e":328.18,"en":"It doesn't take donations and doesn't want to be seen as a charity.","zh":"它不接受捐款，也不希望被视为慈善机构。"},{"s":328.18,"e":343.2,"en":"Mr. Wilson says when people start to know other people around them, they realize they're not that different, and whatever their financial background or their educational background, most people will have something in common with each other.","zh":"Wilson先生说，当人们开始了解周围的其他人时，他们会意识到彼此并不那么不同，无论他们的经济背景或教育背景如何，大多数人都会有共同之处。"},{"s":343.2,"e":446.1,"en":"He says it's important that his cafe can offer his customers security and permanence.","zh":"他说，他的咖啡馆能够为顾客提供安全感和稳定性非常重要。"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-3","label":"长对话 1","questions":"第 8–11 题","start":446.1,"end":622.43,"sentences":[{"s":448.46,"e":452.28,"en":"So what time do you think we should have the party on Saturday?","zh":"那么，你觉得我们周六的派对应该在什么时候举行？"},{"s":452.28,"e":460.14,"en":"How about inviting people to come at 6 p.m.? Then we'll have the afternoon to prepare food and drink and stuff like that.","zh":"邀请大家6点来怎么样？这样我们就有一下午的时间来准备食物、饮料什么的。"},{"s":460.14,"e":463.7,"en":"Yes, I was thinking that around 6 would be good too.","zh":"是的，我也觉得大约6点左右比较好。"},{"s":463.7,"e":465.82,"en":"What food should we provide?","zh":"我们应该提供哪些食物？"},{"s":465.82,"e":469.64,"en":"Well, I had thought about baking a cake and some biscuits.","zh":"嗯，我想过要烤一个蛋糕和一些饼干。"},{"s":469.64,"e":481.7,"en":"And now, I think we should prepare some sandwiches and snacks and some other kinds of food so that people can just help themselves rather than getting everyone to sit down at the table to eat a meal.","zh":"现在，我认为我们应该准备一些三明治、零食和其他食物，这样人们就可以自取食物，而不是让每个人都坐到餐桌旁用餐。"},{"s":481.7,"e":484.1,"en":"I think that's a bit too formal.","zh":"我觉得这有点太正式了。"},{"s":484.1,"e":489.74,"en":"It's better to let people walk around and talk to each other or sit where they like.","zh":"最好让人们四处走动、相互交谈，或者坐在他们喜欢的地方。"},{"s":489.74,"e":491.84,"en":"Yes, that sounds good.","zh":"是的，听起来不错。"},{"s":491.84,"e":494.98,"en":"I'll go to the supermarket to get some drinks.","zh":"我去超市买点饮料。"},{"s":494.98,"e":501.3,"en":"I think I might try that big new supermarket on the other side of town and see what they have.","zh":"我想去城另一边的那个新开的大超市看看，看看他们有什么东西。"},{"s":501.3,"e":503.58,"en":"I've not been there before.","zh":"我以前去过那儿。"},{"s":503.58,"e":509.36,"en":"I think we should get some beer and wine and some fruit juice and other soft drinks.","zh":"我觉得我们应该买些啤酒和葡萄酒，还有一些果汁和其他软饮料。"},{"s":509.36,"e":510.4,"en":"What do you think?","zh":"您觉得如何？"},{"s":510.4,"e":511.46,"en":"Sounds great.","zh":"听起来不错！"},{"s":511.46,"e":513.92,"en":"I think those drinks will be enough.","zh":"我觉得这些饮料就够了。"},{"s":513.92,"e":519.4,"en":"And I heard that the new supermarket offers some big discounts to attract customers.","zh":"我还听说，新开的超市为了吸引顾客，提供了一些很大的折扣。"},{"s":519.4,"e":522.24,"en":"So, going there should be a great idea.","zh":"所以，去那里应该是个好主意。"},{"s":522.24,"e":524.54,"en":"What should we do about music?","zh":"我们该如何处理音乐？"},{"s":524.54,"e":529.86,"en":"Maybe we should ask Paul to bring his computer and speakers so that we can play some music.","zh":"也许我们应该让Paul带上他的电脑和音箱，这样我们就可以放些音乐。"},{"s":529.86,"e":532.7,"en":"He has a great collection of different stuff.","zh":"他收藏了各种各样的东西。"},{"s":532.7,"e":622.43,"en":"Yes, all right.","zh":"好 ， 就是 你"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-4","label":"长对话 2","questions":"第 12–15 题","start":622.43,"end":836.6,"sentences":[{"s":624.21,"e":626.91,"en":"I'm thinking of buying a car.","zh":"我正在考虑买一辆车。"},{"s":626.91,"e":633.55,"en":"I wouldn't need to use it every day, but I think it would be very convenient to have one for the weekends.","zh":"我不需要每天都用，但我觉得周末能有一辆会非常方便。"},{"s":633.55,"e":635.27,"en":"That's exciting.","zh":"聽 起來 很 刺激 吧"},{"s":635.27,"e":637.41,"en":"Would this be your first car?","zh":"这是您的第一辆车吗？"},{"s":637.41,"e":642.35,"en":"No, I actually owned a car for a little while when I lived in Miami.","zh":"不，其实我在迈阿密住的时候有一段时间拥有过一辆车。"},{"s":642.35,"e":650.65,"en":"You see, in America, many cities don't have good public transport, so most people need their own car to get around.","zh":"你看，在美国，很多城市都没有好的公共交通，所以大多数人需要有自己的车才能出行。"},{"s":650.65,"e":652.15,"en":"I see.","zh":"我懂了。"},{"s":652.15,"e":656.25,"en":"So, have you got your mind set on a specific model?","zh":"那么，您是否已经确定了心仪的特定车型？"},{"s":656.25,"e":657.91,"en":"No, not really.","zh":"不,不是真的?"},{"s":657.91,"e":665.35,"en":"I've heard that German cars are very reliable, but I haven't decided on a specific model yet.","zh":"我听说德国车非常可靠，但我还没有决定具体的车型。"},{"s":665.35,"e":670.05,"en":"I'd also like it to be small so that it's easy to drive in the city.","zh":"我也希望它小一点，这样在市区里开起来比较方便。"},{"s":670.05,"e":673.73,"en":"I have a friend who sells second-hand cars.","zh":"我有一个朋友卖二手车。"},{"s":673.73,"e":677.23,"en":"In fact, I think his family owns the business.","zh":"事实上，我认为这家公司是他家人开的。"},{"s":677.23,"e":681.01,"en":"He's a really nice guy, and he knows a lot about cars.","zh":"他是个非常好的人，对汽车非常了解。"},{"s":681.01,"e":687.49,"en":"I could give you his phone number if you want, and you could call him and ask him questions.","zh":"如果您愿意，我可以把他的电话号码给您，您可以给他打电话，向他提问。"},{"s":687.49,"e":693.29,"en":"That's nice of you, but I don't want to feel obliged to buy one of his cars.","zh":"你真好，但我不想觉得有义务买他的车。"},{"s":693.29,"e":695.45,"en":"Oh no, he's not like that.","zh":"哦，不，他不是那样的人。"},{"s":695.45,"e":700.63,"en":"He's a good friend of mine, and he would never try to pressure you or cheat you.","zh":"他是我的好朋友，他绝不会试图施压或欺骗你。"},{"s":700.63,"e":704.87,"en":"Well, if you trust him, then I guess it should be okay.","zh":"好吧，如果你相信他，那我想应该没问题。"},{"s":704.87,"e":711.31,"en":"To be honest, I could use some help in deciding what type of vehicle would best suit my needs.","zh":"老实说，我需要一些帮助来决定哪种类型的车辆最适合我的需求。"},{"s":711.31,"e":714.33,"en":"Speaking to an expert would be a good idea.","zh":"与专家交谈是个好主意。"},{"s":714.33,"e":715.45,"en":"Exactly.","zh":"完全正确。"},{"s":715.45,"e":718.01,"en":"You have nothing to worry about.","zh":"不足为虑。"},{"s":718.01,"e":836.6,"en":"He's a lovely guy, and he'll be happy to help.","zh":"他是个很棒的人，他很乐意帮忙。"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-5","label":"篇章 1","questions":"第 16–18 题","start":836.6,"end":1013.68,"sentences":[{"s":838.52,"e":842.0,"en":"Pigs are not native to North America.","zh":"猪并非北美本土物种。"},{"s":842.0,"e":848.96,"en":"They were first introduced to California by Spanish and Russian explorers and settlers many centuries ago.","zh":"几个世纪前，西班牙和俄罗斯的探险家和定居者首次将它们引入加利福尼亚。"},{"s":848.96,"e":854.38,"en":"In the early times, pigs were allowed to wander freely in search of food.","zh":"在早期，猪可以自由觅食。"},{"s":854.38,"e":861.58,"en":"This practice also allowed many pigs to escape from farms and live in the wild, which became a problem.","zh":"这种做法也导致许多猪从养猪场逃出，在野外生活，这成了一个问题。"},{"s":861.58,"e":867.84,"en":"In fact, they're one of the most damaging invasive species on the continent.","zh":"事实上，它们是该大陆最具破坏性的入侵物种之一。"},{"s":867.84,"e":873.02,"en":"Wild pigs cause millions of dollars in crop damage yearly.","zh":"野猪每年造成数百万美元的作物损失。"},{"s":873.02,"e":879.58,"en":"They also harbour dozens of diseases that threaten both humans and farm animals.","zh":"它们还携带数十种威胁人类和家畜的疾病。"},{"s":879.58,"e":886.48,"en":"Forest patches with wild pigs have been found to have considerably reduced plant and animal diversity.","zh":"研究发现，有野猪出没的林地斑块的植物和动物多样性大大降低。"},{"s":886.48,"e":897.44,"en":"In addition to either eating other animals or their food supply, wild pigs damage native habitats by rooting up grasses and rubbing on trees.","zh":"除了捕食其他动物或抢夺它们的食物外，野猪还会通过拱草和蹭树来破坏原生栖息地。"},{"s":897.44,"e":904.98,"en":"Their activities may also create opportunities for invasive plants to colonise these areas.","zh":"它们的活动也可能为入侵植物在这些地区定殖创造机会。"},{"s":904.98,"e":910.16,"en":"Wild pigs will eat almost anything containing calories.","zh":"野猪几乎什么都吃，只要含有热量。"},{"s":910.16,"e":916.86,"en":"Mice, deer, birds, snakes and frogs are among their victims.","zh":"它们的猎物包括老鼠、鹿、鸟、蛇和青蛙。"},{"s":916.86,"e":925.46,"en":"They can also harm other wild species through indirect competition, rather than eating them or shrinking their food supply.","zh":"它们还可以通过间接竞争来危害其他野生物种，而不是通过捕食或减少其食物供应。"},{"s":925.46,"e":934.8,"en":"On one particular United States island, wild pigs themselves became an attractive food source for a species of mainland eagle.","zh":"在美国的一座岛屿上，野猪本身成为一种大陆鹰类的诱人食物来源。"},{"s":934.8,"e":941.42,"en":"The eagles began breeding on the island and also feeding on a species of native fox.","zh":"秃鹰开始在岛上繁殖，并以一种本土狐狸为食。"},{"s":941.42,"e":1013.68,"en":"The foxes were almost wiped out completely.","zh":"狐狸几乎被彻底消灭了。"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-6","label":"篇章 2","questions":"第 19–21 题","start":1013.68,"end":1180.82,"sentences":[{"s":1015.88,"e":1025.26,"en":"A pair of entrepreneurs are planning to build and launch a spacecraft that would carry and roast coffee beans in outer space.","zh":"两位企业家正计划建造并发射一艘宇宙飞船，用于在太空中运载和烘焙咖啡豆。"},{"s":1025.26,"e":1033.26,"en":"The craft will use the heat of re-entry to roast coffee beans as they float inside it in a pressurised tank.","zh":"该飞行器将利用重返大气层的热量来烘焙漂浮在加压罐内的咖啡豆。"},{"s":1033.26,"e":1039.56,"en":"The effect would be to roast the beans all over and produce perfect coffee.","zh":"这样一来，咖啡豆就能被均匀烘焙，从而酿制出完美的咖啡。"},{"s":1039.56,"e":1057.82,"en":"The businessmen say that on Earth, beans can easily break apart and get burned in the roaster, but if gravity is removed, the beans float around in a heated oven, receive 360 degrees of evenly distributed heat and roast to near perfection.","zh":"这些商人说，在地球上，咖啡豆很容易破碎，并在烘焙机中被烤焦，但如果消除了重力，咖啡豆就会在加热的烘焙机中漂浮，受到360度均匀分布的热量，并被烘焙得近乎完美。"},{"s":1057.82,"e":1062.78,"en":"The spacecraft will reach a height of around 200 kilometres.","zh":"该航天器将达到约200公里的高度。"},{"s":1062.78,"e":1070.24,"en":"The beans would then be roasted in the heat generated by the craft's 20-minute re-entry into Earth's atmosphere.","zh":"然后，咖啡豆将在飞船重返地球大气层20分钟所产生的热量中烘焙。"},{"s":1070.24,"e":1076.28,"en":"Temperatures in the pressurised tank will be kept to around 200 degrees Celsius.","zh":"加压罐内的温度将保持在约200摄氏度。"},{"s":1076.28,"e":1086.24,"en":"Once back on Earth, the planet's first space-roasted beans would be used to make coffee that would be sold for the first time in Dubai.","zh":"返回地球后，这批在太空中烘焙的咖啡豆将用于制作咖啡，并在迪拜首次售卖。"},{"s":1086.24,"e":1089.02,"en":"This is where the pair's company is based.","zh":"这里是这对夫妇的公司所在地。"},{"s":1089.02,"e":1092.42,"en":"It is not clear how much they would charge for a cup.","zh":"目前尚不清楚他们会收取多少钱一杯。"},{"s":1092.42,"e":1100.8,"en":"Surprisingly, the space roaster concept, should it go ahead, will not be the first attempt to take coffee into space.","zh":"令人惊讶的是，如果太空烘焙机概念得以实施，这并不会是首次将咖啡带入太空的尝试。"},{"s":1100.8,"e":1180.82,"en":"In 2015, two Italian companies collaborated on the construction of a similar type of spacecraft, which was the first coffee machine designed for use in space.","zh":"2015年，两家意大利公司合作建造了一艘类似类型的航天器，这是第一台专为在太空中使用而设计的咖啡机。"}]},{"id":"2021-06-1-7","label":"篇章 3","questions":"第 22–25 题","start":1180.82,"end":1382.84,"sentences":[{"s":1182.52,"e":1187.78,"en":"In cold and snowy Alaska, there's a village called Tekotna.","zh":"在寒冷多雪的阿拉斯加，有一个叫特科特纳的村庄。"},{"s":1187.78,"e":1192.04,"en":"It has a population of a mere 49 souls.","zh":"这里只有49位居民。"},{"s":1192.04,"e":1201.14,"en":"Each March, this tiny village swells up in numbers because it is located in the middle of a race that takes place every year.","zh":"每年三月，这个小村庄的人口都会激增，因为它位于每年都会举办的一场赛事的中间地带。"},{"s":1201.14,"e":1212.0,"en":"It is a seven-day race called the Iditarod Trail, and participants stop at Tekotna for their obligatory 24-hour rest.","zh":"这是一场为期七天的比赛，名为爱德华·罗德雪橇犬赛（Iditarod Trail），参赛者会在特科特纳（Tekotna）停留，进行强制性的24小时休息。"},{"s":1212.0,"e":1217.74,"en":"Lucky for them, Tekotna is famous for its delicious fruit pies.","zh":"他们很幸运，因为特科特纳以其美味的水果馅饼而闻名。"},{"s":1217.74,"e":1227.48,"en":"Weeks before the competitors arrive, the residents of Tekotna start preparing for what is without question their biggest event of the year.","zh":"在参赛者抵达前几周，特科特纳的居民就开始为无疑是他们一年中最重要的赛事做准备。"},{"s":1227.48,"e":1235.84,"en":"The whole village chips in to help, including the kids, who end up developing their baking skills at an early age.","zh":"全村人都来帮忙，包括孩子们，他们从小就练就了烘焙的本领。"},{"s":1235.84,"e":1246.6,"en":"The exhausted and hungry racers are greeted with delightful pies of all kinds, such as apple, orange, lemon, or banana.","zh":"筋疲力尽、饥肠辘辘的赛车手们迎来了各种美味的馅饼，如苹果馅饼、橙子馅饼、柠檬馅饼或香蕉馅饼。"},{"s":1246.6,"e":1251.54,"en":"They consume the pies as stomach-warming race fuel.","zh":"他们把馅饼当成暖胃的比赛能量补给。"},{"s":1251.54,"e":1256.64,"en":"The toughness of the race allows for racers to eat pretty much whatever they want.","zh":"比赛的艰苦程度让参赛者可以尽情享用他们想吃的任何东西。"},{"s":1256.64,"e":1259.16,"en":"The more calories, the better.","zh":"卡路里越多越好。"},{"s":1259.16,"e":1265.66,"en":"Tekotna has gained a reputation for its dessert-based hospitality since the 1970s.","zh":"自 20 世纪 70 年代以来，Tekotna 以其以甜点为主的待客之道而闻名。"},{"s":1265.66,"e":1270.1,"en":"It started with one person, Jan Newton.","zh":"一切始于一个人，那就是Jan Newton。"},{"s":1270.1,"e":1276.54,"en":"Jan moved from Idaho with her husband in 1972 and opened a restaurant.","zh":"1972年，Jan与丈夫从爱达荷州搬来，开了一家餐厅。"},{"s":1276.54,"e":1284.48,"en":"Her rich and filling fruit pies quickly got the racers' attention, and the village gained some fame as a result.","zh":"她馅料丰富、口感饱满的水果馅饼很快吸引了车手的注意，村子也因此小有名气。"},{"s":1284.48,"e":1382.84,"en":"Proud residents then started to refer to Jan as Queen of Tekotna.","zh":"自豪的居民们开始称呼简为特科特纳女王。"}]}]},{"id":"2021-12-1","title":"2021年12月 第1套","audio":"listening/2021-12-1.ogg","duration":1409.65,"parts":[{"id":"2021-12-1-0","label":"新闻 1","questions":"第 1–2 题","start":42.42,"end":173.03,"sentences":[{"s":44.14,"e":52.44,"en":"United Airlines has apologized for mistakenly shipping an American family's pet dog thousands of miles in the wrong direction to Japan.","zh":"美联航因将一个美国家庭的宠物狗误运至数千英里外的日本而道歉。"},{"s":52.44,"e":63.56,"en":"The dog owners' beloved 10-year-old dog named Buddy took an unexpected 16-hour flight to Tokyo following a mix-up by the airline.","zh":"由于航空公司的疏忽，狗主人心爱的10岁爱犬Buddy意外搭乘了16小时的航班飞往东京。"},{"s":63.56,"e":67.82,"en":"The dog owners' family are currently in the process of moving.","zh":"狗主人的家人目前正在搬家。"},{"s":67.82,"e":74.18,"en":"They were meant to be reunited with the pet in their new home city in Texas.","zh":"他们本打算在新家所在的德克萨斯州与宠物团聚。"},{"s":74.18,"e":83.28,"en":"But when they arrived at the United Airlines cargo facility in the southern U.S. state, they found a stranger's dog waiting in Buddy's place.","zh":"但当他们抵达美国南部该州的联合航空公司货运设施时，他们发现一只陌生人的狗正站在Buddy的位置上等着。"},{"s":83.28,"e":94.2,"en":"Both of the dogs had been sent to the wrong destinations on connecting flights from Denver, with Buddy mistakenly being sent to Japan instead.","zh":"这两只狗在从丹佛搭乘的转机航班上都被送错了目的地，Buddy被误送到了日本。"},{"s":94.2,"e":99.28,"en":"Buddy was given a physical check-up when he arrived at Tokyo's International Airport.","zh":"巴迪抵达东京国际机场时接受了体检。"},{"s":99.28,"e":104.62,"en":"The dog was then sent back to the U.S. on a private charter jet.","zh":"随后，这只狗搭乘私人包机返回美国。"},{"s":104.62,"e":110.58,"en":"I'm so glad he's alive and coming home soon, said the relieved dog owner.","zh":"“我真高兴他还活着，而且很快就能回家了。”这位如释重负的狗主人说道。"},{"s":110.58,"e":114.02,"en":"An error occurred during the connections in Denver.","zh":"在丹佛转机时发生错误。"},{"s":114.02,"e":118.44,"en":"We have notified our customers that their pets arrived safely.","zh":"我们已通知客户，他们的宠物已安全抵达。"},{"s":118.44,"e":173.03,"en":"We will arrange to return the pets to them as soon as possible, a spokesperson of United Airlines said.","zh":"联合航空的发言人表示，我们将尽快安排将宠物归还给他们。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-1","label":"新闻 2","questions":"第 3–4 题","start":173.03,"end":283.72,"sentences":[{"s":175.07,"e":180.71,"en":"Officials at Reid Park Zoo in Tucson, Arizona are celebrating the birth of a baby elephant.","zh":"亚利桑那州图森市里德公园动物园的工作人员正在庆祝一头小象的诞生。"},{"s":180.71,"e":185.31,"en":"Zoo officials say the baby was born on Monday.","zh":"动物园工作人员表示，这只幼崽于周一出生。"},{"s":185.31,"e":189.93,"en":"It is a female and she weighs nearly 130 kilograms.","zh":"这是一只雌性大熊猫，体重将近130公斤。"},{"s":189.93,"e":194.45,"en":"Semba, her mother, is a 30-year-old African elephant.","zh":"她的母亲森巴是一头30岁的非洲象。"},{"s":194.45,"e":197.63,"en":"The pregnancy lasted 22 months.","zh":"妊娠期持续了22个月。"},{"s":197.63,"e":203.09,"en":"Officials describe the baby elephant as healthy, standing and nursing.","zh":"官员们表示，这头小象很健康，能够站立并吃奶。"},{"s":203.09,"e":206.03,"en":"The baby hasn't been given a name yet.","zh":"这个宝宝还没有取名字。"},{"s":206.03,"e":207.73,"en":"Semba has given birth before.","zh":"森芭以前生过孩子。"},{"s":207.73,"e":215.89,"en":"Zoo officials said during this pregnancy she was closely monitored through physical exams and blood tests.","zh":"动物园工作人员表示，在怀孕期间，她通过体检和血液检查受到密切监测。"},{"s":215.89,"e":221.49,"en":"Dr. Sue Tagielski is the zoo's director of zoological operations.","zh":"Sue Tagielski博士是动物园的动物事务总监。"},{"s":221.49,"e":227.19,"en":"She said the elephant's birth went smoothly and that there were no complications.","zh":"她说，大象的生产过程很顺利，没有出现任何并发症。"},{"s":227.19,"e":231.05,"en":"The new baby expands the zoo's elephant herd to six.","zh":"这只新生幼崽使动物园的大象群增加到六只。"},{"s":231.05,"e":283.72,"en":"That includes the baby's parents, a sister, a brother and an adult female.","zh":"其中包括婴儿的父母、一个妹妹、一个哥哥和一个成年女性。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-2","label":"新闻 3","questions":"第 5–7 题","start":283.72,"end":449.26,"sentences":[{"s":285.64,"e":290.12,"en":"Three years ago, a couple was enjoying a meal at a beach restaurant.","zh":"三年前，一对夫妇正在一家海滩餐厅用餐。"},{"s":290.12,"e":294.28,"en":"The restaurant was built on a wooden structure above the seawater.","zh":"这家餐厅建在海面上的木质结构之上。"},{"s":294.28,"e":299.56,"en":"During the meal, the man's wedding ring slipped off his finger.","zh":"用餐时，男子的结婚戒指从手指上滑落。"},{"s":299.56,"e":304.1,"en":"It fell through the wooden floorboards, apparently lost forever.","zh":"它掉进了木地板的缝隙里，显然是永远地消失了。"},{"s":304.1,"e":309.62,"en":"Recently, the restaurant manager, Ryan Cravoy, decided to replace the wooden deck.","zh":"最近，餐厅经理Ryan Cravoy决定更换木质露台。"},{"s":309.62,"e":317.6,"en":"And he found an old gold coin, some $100 bills and a silver wedding ring while replacing the deck.","zh":"他在更换地板时发现了一枚古老的金币、一些100美元的钞票和一枚银质结婚戒指。"},{"s":317.6,"e":322.62,"en":"The restaurant's waitress, Sasha Formica, posted a picture of the ring on Facebook.","zh":"餐厅的服务员萨沙·福米卡（Sasha Formica）在Facebook上发布了这枚戒指的照片。"},{"s":322.62,"e":326.94,"en":"The post was shared about 5,000 times.","zh":"该帖被分享了约5000次。"},{"s":326.94,"e":330.9,"en":"Three days later, the happy wife called to claim the ring.","zh":"三天后，这位喜出望外的妻子打电话来认领戒指。"},{"s":330.9,"e":337.72,"en":"She even texted pictures of her and her husband eating there in 2017 as proof.","zh":"她甚至发来了2017年她和丈夫在那里用餐的照片作为证据。"},{"s":337.72,"e":341.36,"en":"The restaurant mailed the ring back to the happy couple.","zh":"餐厅将戒指寄回给了这对幸福的夫妇。"},{"s":341.36,"e":346.2,"en":"Meanwhile, Cravoy discovered that the gold coin was very rare.","zh":"与此同时，克拉沃伊发现这枚金币非常罕见。"},{"s":346.2,"e":449.26,"en":"It was from 1855 and worth as much as $2,000.","zh":"它产于1855年，价值高达2000美元。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-3","label":"长对话 1","questions":"第 8–11 题","start":449.26,"end":652.35,"sentences":[{"s":451.08,"e":456.36,"en":"I can't believe that duck hunting is still legal in so many parts of the world.","zh":"我真不敢相信，在世界上这么多地方，猎鸭竟然还是合法的。"},{"s":456.36,"e":465.44,"en":"The scientific evidence from countries like Australia, Canada, and the USA clearly indicates a decline in the birds' numbers.","zh":"来自澳大利亚、加拿大和美国等国家的科学证据清楚地表明，鸟类的数量正在减少。"},{"s":465.44,"e":472.14,"en":"But can anyone be sure if the decline is really caused by the hunting or by climate change?","zh":"但是，有人能确定这种下降真的是由狩猎造成的，还是由气候变化造成的吗？"},{"s":472.14,"e":474.2,"en":"It's caused by both, in fact.","zh":"实际上，两者都会导致这种情况。"},{"s":474.2,"e":478.34,"en":"We see more droughts in countries like Australia.","zh":"在澳大利亚等国家，我们看到干旱更加频繁。"},{"s":478.34,"e":484.04,"en":"Ducks are birds that feed and breed in areas where there is a lot of water.","zh":"鸭子是在水源丰富的地方觅食和繁殖的鸟类。"},{"s":484.04,"e":489.54,"en":"But their habitats have been shrinking in recent decades because of the droughts.","zh":"但近几十年来，由于干旱，它们的栖息地一直在萎缩。"},{"s":489.54,"e":495.44,"en":"And I guess with fewer places to inhabit, they concentrate in greater numbers in fewer areas.","zh":"我想，由于可居住的地方变少了，它们会集中在更少的区域，数量也更多。"},{"s":495.44,"e":499.0,"en":"Which surely makes them easier targets for the hunters.","zh":"这当然使它们更容易成为猎人的目标。"},{"s":499.0,"e":500.24,"en":"It does.","zh":"政治对管理很重要。"},{"s":500.24,"e":501.96,"en":"My grandfather was a duck hunter.","zh":"我爷爷是个猎鸭人。"},{"s":501.96,"e":507.24,"en":"He told me hunting ducks and geese began in the 19th century.","zh":"他告诉我，狩猎鸭子和鹅的活动始于 19 世纪。"},{"s":507.24,"e":515.26,"en":"They were an easily found and plentifully available food source in farming areas, especially for poor immigrants.","zh":"在农业地区，它们是一种很容易找到且供应充足的食物来源，对于贫困移民来说尤其如此。"},{"s":515.26,"e":518.34,"en":"What did they use for hunting during that period?","zh":"在那个时期，他们用什么来狩猎？"},{"s":518.34,"e":523.58,"en":"They used new types of guns, and birds could easily be shot down in flight.","zh":"他们使用了新型枪械，鸟儿在飞行中很容易被击落。"},{"s":523.58,"e":529.04,"en":"And in such great numbers that commercial hunting of ducks and geese became an industry.","zh":"而且数量之多，以至于对鸭子和鹅的商业性捕猎成为了一项产业。"},{"s":529.04,"e":533.58,"en":"Yet there's no commercial farming of these birds nowadays.","zh":"然而，如今已经没有对这些鸟类的商业养殖了。"},{"s":533.58,"e":537.32,"en":"Their meat is hardly eaten in Western countries.","zh":"在西方国家，人们很少食用它们的肉。"},{"s":537.32,"e":538.04,"en":"No.","zh":"序号"},{"s":538.04,"e":542.86,"en":"Duck hunting seemingly exists as the continuation of a tradition.","zh":"狩猎野鸭似乎是延续一项传统。"},{"s":542.86,"e":549.84,"en":"Wild ducks have never been popular with farmers like my grandfather anyway, because they sometimes destroy crops.","zh":"反正，像我爷爷这样的农民从来都不喜欢野鸭，因为它们有时会毁坏庄稼。"},{"s":549.84,"e":553.58,"en":"In fact, farmers use to poison them in large numbers.","zh":"事实上，农民过去经常大量使用毒药来对付它们。"},{"s":553.58,"e":556.14,"en":"That somehow doesn't surprise me.","zh":"这倒不让我感到意外。"},{"s":556.14,"e":652.35,"en":"Nobody places much value on the lives of these poor birds or on their meat.","zh":"没有人太看重这些可怜的鸟的性命，也不太看重它们的肉。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-4","label":"长对话 2","questions":"第 12–15 题","start":652.35,"end":885.73,"sentences":[{"s":654.21,"e":655.43,"en":"OK, Miss Bright.","zh":"好的，布莱特小姐。"},{"s":655.43,"e":657.49,"en":"I've finished calculating.","zh":"我算完了。"},{"s":657.49,"e":664.21,"en":"I estimate you have between 210 and 240 square metres of walls and ceiling.","zh":"我估计您的墙壁和天花板面积在210至240平方米之间。"},{"s":664.21,"e":666.97,"en":"So, how much would the paint job cost?","zh":"那么，喷漆要花多少钱？"},{"s":666.97,"e":671.21,"en":"That would depend on the quality of paint you choose.","zh":"这取决于您选择的涂料质量。"},{"s":671.21,"e":673.19,"en":"We carry two brands.","zh":"我们经营两个品牌。"},{"s":673.19,"e":678.55,"en":"One costs 60 cents every square metre and the other 90 cents.","zh":"一种每平方米60美分，另一种90美分。"},{"s":678.55,"e":687.61,"en":"The second is guaranteed to look great for about 10 years, whereas the cheaper one will start to dull after around 6 or 7 years.","zh":"后者保证在约10年内保持良好外观，而较便宜的后者在约6或7年后就会开始失去光泽。"},{"s":687.61,"e":691.79,"en":"In that case, we would prefer the more expensive option.","zh":"在这种情况下，我们更倾向于选择价格更高的选项。"},{"s":691.79,"e":693.83,"en":"Alright then.","zh":"那好吧……"},{"s":693.83,"e":700.51,"en":"So, including labour costs, taxes and everything, this job would come to $3,000.","zh":"因此，包括劳动力成本、税收和所有费用，这份工作的收入将达到3,000美元。"},{"s":700.51,"e":701.53,"en":"Hmm.","zh":"唔。"},{"s":701.53,"e":706.21,"en":"To be perfectly honest, that's more than I expected.","zh":"说实话，这比我预期的。"},{"s":706.21,"e":713.51,"en":"Please bear in mind that the price includes moving all the furniture and the whole task would take two days.","zh":"请注意，价格包括搬动所有家具和整个任务需要两天时间。"},{"s":713.51,"e":714.37,"en":"Really?","zh":"真的吗？"},{"s":714.37,"e":715.45,"en":"Why?","zh":"为什么？"},{"s":715.45,"e":724.51,"en":"Well, we can't paint the walls without clearing all the furniture first, so every time we paint a room, we first have to move the furniture to another room.","zh":"嗯，我们不能不清理就粉刷墙壁先把所有的家具都摆上，所以每次我们粉刷房间，我们首先要搬家把家具搬到另一个房间。"},{"s":724.51,"e":726.57,"en":"So that takes more time.","zh":"所以这需要更多时间。"},{"s":726.57,"e":730.61,"en":"Plus it requires two people, which works out more expensive.","zh":"另外，它需要两个人，更贵。"},{"s":730.61,"e":731.77,"en":"I see.","zh":"我懂了。"},{"s":731.77,"e":736.83,"en":"But does that mean I could not live here in my own house during those two days?","zh":"但这是否意味着我无法活下去在那两次天？"},{"s":736.83,"e":738.61,"en":"That is correct.","zh":"正确。"},{"s":738.61,"e":739.71,"en":"Oh well.","zh":"那好吧。"},{"s":739.71,"e":742.27,"en":"That changes everything, I'm afraid.","zh":"我担心那会改变一切。"},{"s":742.27,"e":745.83,"en":"I would have to stay with a friend or check into a hotel.","zh":"我必须和朋友住在一起或入住酒店。"},{"s":745.83,"e":748.05,"en":"I hadn't considered any of that.","zh":"我之前根本没考虑过这些。"},{"s":748.05,"e":755.11,"en":"I'm starting to realize that painting my house is far more troublesome than I had anticipated.","zh":"我开始意识到粉刷我的房子比我预想的要麻烦得多。"},{"s":755.11,"e":757.11,"en":"This is usually the case.","zh":"通常情况都是这样的。"},{"s":757.11,"e":760.55,"en":"Most of our clients go through the same realization.","zh":"我们的大多数客户都经历过同样的实现。"},{"s":760.55,"e":761.93,"en":"I see.","zh":"我懂了。"},{"s":761.93,"e":763.43,"en":"You have my number.","zh":"你有我的电话号码。"},{"s":763.43,"e":767.45,"en":"Please feel free to call me for any further questions.","zh":"如有任何疑问，请随时给我打电话进一步的问题。"},{"s":767.45,"e":885.73,"en":"Thank you.","zh":"谢谢。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-5","label":"篇章 1","questions":"第 16–18 题","start":885.73,"end":1055.38,"sentences":[{"s":887.35,"e":896.29,"en":"Homework is an important part of schooling, but the purposes of giving children homework will change as they grow older.","zh":"家庭作业是学校教育的重要组成部分，但是给孩子布置家庭作业的目的将会改变随着他们长大。"},{"s":896.29,"e":905.41,"en":"At the primary level, the main aim is to cultivate good habits, like learning to plan and exercising self-discipline.","zh":"在小学阶段，主要目标是培养良好的习惯，比如学会计划并加强自律。"},{"s":905.41,"e":916.65,"en":"During the secondary school years, extending what is learned at school is positively related to academic achievement, so the content of homework becomes more important.","zh":"在中学阶段，延长在学校学到的知识与学业成绩呈正相关成绩，所以家庭作业的内容变得更加重要的。"},{"s":916.65,"e":920.53,"en":"So how can you help your child do their best?","zh":"那么你怎样才能帮助你的孩子他们最好的？"},{"s":920.53,"e":926.89,"en":"Creating an ideal working environment will make it easier for them to get down to their assignments quickly.","zh":"创造理想的工作环境将使让他们更容易地投入到他们的快速完成作业。"},{"s":926.89,"e":937.69,"en":"Make sure it's free of distractions, and for primary school children at least, somewhere near you, so you can answer questions and offer encouragement.","zh":"确保没有干扰，并且至少在你附近某个地方的小学生，这样你就可以回答问题并提供鼓励。"},{"s":937.69,"e":947.37,"en":"You'll probably have to help younger children plan their session, but it's important that by the end of primary school, it's second nature.","zh":"你可能必须帮助年幼的孩子计划他们的会议，但重要的是，小学毕业后，它就成了第二天性。"},{"s":947.37,"e":954.97,"en":"Get them to tell you everything they have to do, then encourage them to establish an order in which they do work.","zh":"让他们告诉你他们所拥有的一切然后鼓励他们建立一个他们工作的顺序。"},{"s":954.97,"e":962.57,"en":"When there's several different assignments, make sure they begin with one they enjoy, so it seems easy to get started.","zh":"当有几项不同的任务时，确保它们从他们喜欢的开始，所以看起来容易上手。"},{"s":962.57,"e":971.25,"en":"It's best to take on the most difficult task second, once they're settled, but before they get tired.","zh":"最好接受最困难的事情第二项任务，一旦他们安顿下来，但在他们累了。"},{"s":971.25,"e":978.81,"en":"If older children have more than an hour of homework, encourage them to schedule a short break to stretch.","zh":"如果年龄较大的孩子有超过一小时的家庭作业，鼓励他们安排一个简短的休息一下，伸展一下。"},{"s":978.81,"e":1055.38,"en":"If you encourage them to tell you what they've learned, they'll absorb the information more deeply and remember it more readily.","zh":"如果你鼓励他们告诉你什么他们将会更深入地吸收信息并且更容易记住。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-6","label":"篇章 2","questions":"第 19–21 题","start":1055.38,"end":1224.98,"sentences":[{"s":1056.98,"e":1067.1,"en":"Workers at Mexican Oil Company will receive a health incentive of almost $300 a year if they meet certain body weight standards.","zh":"墨西哥石油公司的工人将获得每年近300美元的健康奖励，如果他们符合一定的体重标准。"},{"s":1067.1,"e":1071.52,"en":"To qualify for the bonus, they must maintain a healthy weight.","zh":"要获得奖金，他们必须保持健康的体重。"},{"s":1071.52,"e":1079.54,"en":"For those who are overweight or obese, they can receive the bonus if they reduce their weight by 10% during the year.","zh":"对于那些超重或肥胖的人来说，他们如果他们减少年内减轻体重10%。"},{"s":1079.54,"e":1090.24,"en":"Some applaud the policy as fair because it rewards both individuals who maintain a healthy weight and those who are working towards achieving it.","zh":"一些人称赞该政策公平，因为奖励那些保持健康体重的人以及那些为实现这一目标而努力的人们。"},{"s":1090.24,"e":1101.8,"en":"But critics say the policy contradicts recommendations by many health experts, who warn that a person's weight is influenced by genetic and environmental factors.","zh":"但批评人士表示，该政策与许多健康专家警告说，一个人的体重受遗传和环境因素的影响。"},{"s":1101.8,"e":1107.7,"en":"That means weight can be hard for individuals to control, which makes the bonus unfair.","zh":"这意味着体重对于个人来说可能很难控制，这使得奖金变得不公平。"},{"s":1107.7,"e":1116.62,"en":"Some experts say the policy is inconsistent with the science of what we know about body weight regulation.","zh":"一些专家表示，该政策不符合我们所知的身体科学体重调节。"},{"s":1116.62,"e":1121.3,"en":"These experts argue that focusing on weight is the wrong approach.","zh":"这些专家认为，关注体重是错误的方法。"},{"s":1121.3,"e":1127.96,"en":"A more productive method of encouraging health among employees is to promote healthy behaviors.","zh":"促进健康的更有效方法员工的根本目的是促进健康行为。"},{"s":1127.96,"e":1136.44,"en":"For example, companies can give workers gym memberships or encourage participation in lectures on healthy eating and living.","zh":"例如，公司可以为员工提供健身会员资格或鼓励参加健康饮食讲座和生活。"},{"s":1136.44,"e":1144.58,"en":"They can also reduce sweets and provide healthier snacks in the office and healthier meals at the company canteen.","zh":"它们还可以减少甜食，提供更健康的办公室里的零食和更健康的膳食公司食堂。"},{"s":1144.58,"e":1149.76,"en":"Or they can give employees more time during their lunch break to exercise.","zh":"或者他们可以在午休时间锻炼身体。"},{"s":1149.76,"e":1224.98,"en":"These are much better and much more productive ways for companies to move forward on their employees' well-being.","zh":"这些更好，更高效企业继续前进的方式员工的福祉。"}]},{"id":"2021-12-1-7","label":"篇章 3","questions":"第 22–25 题","start":1224.98,"end":1409.65,"sentences":[{"s":1226.68,"e":1234.34,"en":"Campaigners have warned that the British government is not doing enough to prevent left-handed pupils from falling behind their peers.","zh":"活动人士警告称，英国政府在预防左撇子学生方面做得不够避免落后于同龄人。"},{"s":1234.34,"e":1240.44,"en":"They claim that thousands of children are still being penalized for being left-handed.","zh":"他们声称，仍有数千名儿童因是左撇子而受到惩罚。"},{"s":1240.44,"e":1247.78,"en":"This is due to a lack of action from ministers who have failed to take any meaningful action for years.","zh":"这是由于缺乏行动未能采取任何行动的部长多年来有意义的行动。"},{"s":1247.78,"e":1259.9,"en":"It is feared that a failure to address early year challenges, such as poor handwriting, leads to much more serious problems down the line with these pupils facing reduced career prospects.","zh":"人们担心，如果不能解决早期面临的挑战，例如书写不规范，导致导致更严重的问题这些学生面临的职业前景较差。"},{"s":1259.9,"e":1271.4,"en":"Studies in recent years show that left-handed children are more likely to suffer with learning difficulties and their scores are lower on IQ tests.","zh":"近年来的研究表明，左撇子儿童更有可能学习困难困难，智商得分较低測試。"},{"s":1271.4,"e":1278.88,"en":"Campaigners feel it's strange that children in British schools are penalized because they happen to be left-handed.","zh":"活动人士认为，英国儿童学校受到惩罚，因为他们恰好左撇子。"},{"s":1278.88,"e":1283.82,"en":"They don't understand why successive governments have failed to act on this.","zh":"他们不明白为什么历届政府都失败了并采取行动。"},{"s":1283.82,"e":1295.64,"en":"They want the Department of Education to record which children are left-handed and what their educational attainments are, since they make up some 10% of the population.","zh":"他们希望教育部记录哪些孩子是左撇子，他们的教育水平是10%的人口。"},{"s":1295.64,"e":1302.78,"en":"In early year education, left-handed children are struggling and making a mess of their handwriting.","zh":"在早期教育中，左撇子儿童挣扎并弄乱了他们的笔迹。"},{"s":1302.78,"e":1306.06,"en":"Educators don't know how to deal with this.","zh":"教育工作者不知道该如何处理这个问题。"},{"s":1306.06,"e":1310.5,"en":"In many cases, there's no active help and a lack of teacher training.","zh":"在许多情况下，没有主动的帮助和缺乏教师培训。"},{"s":1310.5,"e":1317.16,"en":"Campaigners point out that a high percentage of the prison population is left-handed.","zh":"活动人士指出，监狱里的囚犯都是左撇子。"},{"s":1317.16,"e":1409.65,"en":"They say that these prison numbers are unusually high and ask why it is the case.","zh":"他们说，这些囚犯人数异常并询问为什么会这样。"}]}]},{"id":"2022-12-1","title":"2022年12月 第1套","audio":"listening/2022-12-1.ogg","duration":1411.45,"parts":[{"id":"2022-12-1-0","label":"新闻 1","questions":"第 1–2 题","start":38.44,"end":155.86,"sentences":[{"s":40.64,"e":50.84,"en":"Operations at one of Australia's largest gold mines had to be temporarily suspended on Friday after a partial wall collapse at one of the mine's dams.","zh":"澳大利亚最大的金矿之一的运营周五不得不暂时停课，因为其中一个地方的墙壁部分倒塌我的水坝。"},{"s":50.84,"e":59.68,"en":"The wall collapse at the Cadia Mine came just a few days after two earthquakes hit the area.","zh":"卡迪亚矿井墙壁倒塌就在两次地震发生几天后該區域。"},{"s":59.68,"e":70.84,"en":"The damage to the dam wall was noticed in the late afternoon on Friday when workers found a section of the northern dam wall had collapsed into the southern dam.","zh":"大坝墙体受损情况引人注目周五下午晚些时候，工人们发现了北坝墙的一部分已经坍塌至南侧大坝。"},{"s":70.84,"e":78.62,"en":"The dams contain waste products of mining and can contain materials which are harmful to the environment and human health.","zh":"水坝中含有采矿产生的废料和可能含有对人体有害的物质环境和人类健康。"},{"s":78.62,"e":86.64,"en":"The dams are generally constructed using earth fill and are gradually raised over time.","zh":"水坝一般采用土石方建造并随着时间的推移逐渐升高。"},{"s":86.64,"e":97.84,"en":"The company was unable to confirm whether the recent earthquakes had contributed to the dam's wall collapse but said it was conducting a thorough investigation.","zh":"该公司无法确认最近的地震对大坝的墙体造成了影响但表示正在进行彻底的调查。"},{"s":97.84,"e":155.86,"en":"A company spokesperson said that operations at the site had been halted while the investigation is ongoing and that the break had posed no safety threat to workers.","zh":"该公司发言人表示，该网站已暂停调查正在进行，而且这次中断并没有造成对工人的安全威胁。"}]},{"id":"2022-12-1-1","label":"新闻 2","questions":"第 3–4 题","start":155.86,"end":467.38,"sentences":[{"s":158.06,"e":166.96,"en":"Two boys and four girls were born on Monday to the surprise of a young couple and doctors who had expected five babies.","zh":"两名男孩和四名女孩出生周一，一对年轻夫妇大吃一惊以及预期有五个孩子的医生。"},{"s":166.96,"e":173.24,"en":"This was the first record of six babies being born at the same time in that region.","zh":"这是第一个六胎婴儿的记录同时出生在那个地区。"},{"s":173.24,"e":179.72,"en":"The doctors prepared from early in the morning to help deliver five tiny citizens.","zh":"医生们从一大早就开始准备帮助接生五位小公民。"},{"s":179.72,"e":184.7,"en":"They were in the operating room with five teams of doctors, one for each baby.","zh":"他们在手术室里，有五个人一组医生，负责每个婴儿。"},{"s":184.7,"e":192.3,"en":"The first five babies were delivered successfully and all baby beds were occupied.","zh":"前五名婴儿均顺利出生，所有婴儿床都被占了。"},{"s":192.3,"e":198.4,"en":"And then, all of a sudden, it turned out there was another waiting to come out.","zh":"然后，突然间，一切都变了外面还有另外一个人在等着出来。"},{"s":198.4,"e":204.52,"en":"The doctors said the babies were in healthy condition but could not go home immediately.","zh":"医生说，婴儿身体健康但不能立即回家。"},{"s":204.52,"e":210.4,"en":"They needed to stay in the hospital for two to three months for medical supervision.","zh":"他们需要住院进行两到三个月的医疗监督。"},{"s":210.4,"e":219.5,"en":"The mother, who was in stable condition, could return home a day later if all physical tests came back normal.","zh":"母亲目前情况稳定，如果身体一切正常，请晚一天回家测试结果恢复正常。"},{"s":219.5,"e":229.6,"en":"The baby's mother commented that they had already prepared room for five babies at home, so they will have to rearrange things for their happy surprise.","zh":"婴儿的母亲表示，他们已经在家里为五个婴儿准备了房间，所以他们将不得不重新安排他们的惊喜。"},{"s":229.6,"e":237.06,"en":"The new parents have yet to name the sixth baby but are considering either Lily or Rose.","zh":"新父母尚未命名第六个孩子，但正在考虑莉莉或玫瑰。"},{"s":237.06,"e":282.48,"en":"Questions three and four are based on the news report you have just heard.","zh":"问题三和问题四基于您刚刚听到的新闻报道。"},{"s":282.48,"e":290.46,"en":"A Spanish island called Palmador has been bought by a family from Europe for 18 million euros.","zh":"西班牙帕尔马多尔岛已被购买来自欧洲的一个家庭以1800万美元的价格欧元。"},{"s":290.46,"e":295.68,"en":"The island is often described as heaven on earth by holiday makers.","zh":"该岛经常被描述为度假者的地球。"},{"s":295.68,"e":303.2,"en":"For decades, tourists have been flocking to Palmador, which is located off the southeast coast of Spain.","zh":"几十年来，游客们纷纷涌向帕尔马多，位于西班牙。"},{"s":303.2,"e":308.82,"en":"They come to enjoy its unspoiled beaches and crystal clear waters.","zh":"他们来这里享受未受污染的海滩和清澈的海水。"},{"s":308.82,"e":313.7,"en":"Its natural beauty is protected as it lies inside a natural park.","zh":"它的自然美景受到保护在自然公园内。"},{"s":313.7,"e":324.28,"en":"Although Palmador is one of the most famous private islands in the world, its seafront is public land and is a favorite destination for famous people.","zh":"尽管Palmador是最著名的世界上的私人岛屿，其海滨是公共土地，是名人。"},{"s":324.28,"e":332.46,"en":"When the island was put up for sale, it was offered to the local government but proved too expensive for the local authorities.","zh":"当这座岛被挂牌出售时，它被提供给当地政府，但这对当地政府来说成本太高。"},{"s":332.46,"e":344.14,"en":"It is unclear whether the new owners have the power to ban tourists from the island, but with their newfound luxury comes the responsibility for its protection and maintenance.","zh":"目前尚不清楚新东家是否禁止游客进入该岛的权力，但随着他们新获得的奢华而来的是责任以便对其进行保护和维护。"},{"s":344.14,"e":349.36,"en":"The island is less than two miles long and half a mile wide.","zh":"该岛长度不到两英里宽半英里。"},{"s":349.36,"e":358.32,"en":"It is said to have a remarkable location that few other private islands of this size can match, according to estate agents.","zh":"据说它有一个非凡的地理位置很少有其他私人岛屿能达到这种规模据房地产经纪人称，可以匹配。"},{"s":358.32,"e":467.38,"en":"Palmador is the perfect place to retreat to, somewhere to get away from the city noise and relax in beautiful surroundings with zero stress.","zh":"Palmador是完美的休憩之地，远离城市喧嚣的地方并在毫无压力的美丽环境中放松身心。"}]},{"id":"2022-12-1-2","label":"长对话 1","questions":"第 8–11 题","start":467.38,"end":647.87,"sentences":[{"s":468.8,"e":469.54,"en":"Hi.","zh":"你好。"},{"s":469.54,"e":470.82,"en":"Christie's Gym Center.","zh":"克里斯蒂健身中心。"},{"s":470.82,"e":472.32,"en":"How can I help you?","zh":"我怎么帮你？"},{"s":472.32,"e":472.98,"en":"Hi.","zh":"你好。"},{"s":472.98,"e":476.66,"en":"I'm calling to ask about the newly scheduled gym classes.","zh":"我打电话来询问新安排的体育课。"},{"s":476.66,"e":479.38,"en":"I'm just wondering if I can get a discount on them.","zh":"我只是想知道我是否可以得到一个折扣。"},{"s":479.38,"e":481.22,"en":"Are you already a member?","zh":"您已经是会员了吗？"},{"s":481.22,"e":481.9,"en":"Yes.","zh":"是的。"},{"s":481.9,"e":486.66,"en":"I signed up two months ago, but I haven't been to any of the group classes yet.","zh":"我两个月前就报名了，但是没有参加过任何小组课程然而。"},{"s":486.66,"e":488.36,"en":"Can I take your name, please?","zh":"可以给我你的名字吗？"},{"s":488.36,"e":488.9,"en":"Yes.","zh":"是的。"},{"s":488.9,"e":491.2,"en":"My name is Carol Friedman.","zh":"我叫卡罗尔弗里德曼。"},{"s":491.2,"e":492.48,"en":"Carol Friedman.","zh":"卡罗尔·弗里德曼。"},{"s":492.48,"e":493.3,"en":"That's right.","zh":"这是正确的。"},{"s":493.3,"e":494.88,"en":"And you signed up two months ago.","zh":"您两个月前就报名了。"},{"s":494.88,"e":504.68,"en":"Currently, we are offering existing members discounts off two of our brand new classes, Hot Yoga and Advanced Spinning.","zh":"目前，我们为现有会员提供折扣我们的两个全新课程，热瑜伽和高级纺纱。"},{"s":504.68,"e":509.3,"en":"But the discount doesn't apply to any of our regular classes, I'm afraid.","zh":"但折扣不适用于任何恐怕我们的常规课程。"},{"s":509.3,"e":512.08,"en":"I'm only interested in the new classes.","zh":"我只对新课程感兴趣。"},{"s":512.08,"e":516.83,"en":"So, how much of a discount is there on these two new classes?","zh":"那么，折扣有多少呢关于这两个新课程？"},{"s":516.83,"e":525.82,"en":"The same discount of 20% is being offered to everyone at the door on a first-come, first-served basis for the first month.","zh":"同样20%的折扣为在门口的每个人提供先到先得月。"},{"s":525.82,"e":528.58,"en":"It's a shame you missed out on the general discount.","zh":"很遗憾你错过了普惠折扣。"},{"s":528.58,"e":529.64,"en":"I see.","zh":"我懂了。"},{"s":529.64,"e":534.56,"en":"But you can get 25% off if you sign up in advance.","zh":"但如果你提前报名。"},{"s":534.56,"e":537.08,"en":"Which of the two classes are you thinking about?","zh":"你想的是这两门课中的哪一门关于？"},{"s":537.08,"e":541.28,"en":"Well, I guess I am only really interested in Hot Yoga.","zh":"嗯，我想我只是真的感兴趣在热瑜伽中。"},{"s":541.28,"e":545.22,"en":"Can you sign me up for the 10-week course on Thursday evenings?","zh":"你能帮我报名参加10周四晚上有为期一周的课程吗？"},{"s":545.22,"e":546.16,"en":"Sure.","zh":"当然。"},{"s":546.16,"e":548.3,"en":"Would you prefer to pay in advance?","zh":"您希望提前付款吗？"},{"s":548.3,"e":552.44,"en":"No, I don't like giving my card details over the phone anyway.","zh":"不，我不喜欢提供我的银行卡信息无论如何，通过电话。"},{"s":552.44,"e":553.54,"en":"Okay then.","zh":"好的。"},{"s":553.54,"e":558.64,"en":"As you are already a member, the fee for the class will just be added to your monthly bill.","zh":"由于您已经是会员，因为该类将被添加到您的每月账单。"},{"s":558.64,"e":559.76,"en":"That's perfect.","zh":"那很完美。"},{"s":559.76,"e":560.94,"en":"Thanks for your help.","zh":"感谢您的帮助。"},{"s":560.94,"e":647.87,"en":"See you Thursday.","zh":"星期四见。"}]},{"id":"2022-12-1-3","label":"长对话 2","questions":"第 12–15 题","start":647.87,"end":1042.1,"sentences":[{"s":649.31,"e":653.25,"en":"Well, I think that was quite a successful trip in the end.","zh":"嗯，我认为那是一个相当成功的最终的旅行。"},{"s":653.25,"e":654.57,"en":"Don't you think, Jenny?","zh":"你不这么认为吗，珍妮？"},{"s":654.57,"e":655.79,"en":"Absolutely.","zh":"绝对地。"},{"s":655.79,"e":658.87,"en":"There are lots of great potential markets here in China.","zh":"这里有很多巨大的潜在市场在中国。"},{"s":658.87,"e":665.77,"en":"So, I'm sure that the head office in London will be pleased once we get back and present our research.","zh":"所以，我确信总部一旦我们回来，伦敦会很高兴并展示我们的研究成果。"},{"s":665.77,"e":666.63,"en":"Okay.","zh":"好的。"},{"s":666.63,"e":668.87,"en":"We've got a bit of spare time now.","zh":"我们现在有一些空闲时间。"},{"s":668.87,"e":671.61,"en":"Can we discuss the return trip to the head office?","zh":"我们可以讨论一下返回总公司？"},{"s":671.61,"e":672.53,"en":"Sure.","zh":"当然。"},{"s":672.53,"e":678.85,"en":"I've checked the availability of flights from Beijing to London on the 22nd, and you have a choice.","zh":"我查了一下从北京出发的航班22号去伦敦，你有一个选择。"},{"s":678.85,"e":690.63,"en":"There's a flight arriving the following morning with a two-hour stopover in Dubai, or a flight arriving at 11.30 in the evening with a five-hour stopover in Amsterdam.","zh":"第二天早上有一班航班抵达在迪拜停留两小时，或者航班于晚上11:30抵达在阿姆斯特丹停留五个小时。"},{"s":690.63,"e":691.33,"en":"Right.","zh":"正确的。"},{"s":691.33,"e":694.07,"en":"Well, that's obvious then, isn't it?","zh":"那么，这很明显，不是吗？"},{"s":694.07,"e":696.13,"en":"Okay, so that's Dubai.","zh":"好的，这就是迪拜。"},{"s":696.13,"e":699.53,"en":"I've booked a room in a hotel about a mile from the office.","zh":"我在酒店预订了房间距办公室一英里。"},{"s":699.53,"e":703.23,"en":"The nearest metro station is Earls Court.","zh":"最近的地铁站是EarlsCourt。"},{"s":703.23,"e":704.35,"en":"Great.","zh":"伟大的。"},{"s":704.35,"e":709.23,"en":"Can you find a map that shows where the hotel is and send it to me online?","zh":"你能找到一张显示哪里的地图吗酒店是，然后发给我在线的？"},{"s":709.23,"e":712.05,"en":"I've never been to the head office, you know.","zh":"我从来没有去过总部，你知道。"},{"s":712.05,"e":718.05,"en":"I want to see if I can get one of those rental bicycles and ride to the office, just for fun.","zh":"我想看看我能否得到租一辆自行车，骑到办公室，只是为了好玩。"},{"s":718.05,"e":723.45,"en":"For the presentation, I'll bring my own laptop and hook it up to their projector.","zh":"为了演讲，我会带上自己的笔记本电脑并将其连接到投影仪上。"},{"s":723.45,"e":726.31,"en":"Do you remember the capacity of their meeting room?","zh":"你还记得他们会议的容量吗房间？"},{"s":726.31,"e":728.19,"en":"No, but I'll check.","zh":"没有，但我会检查一下。"},{"s":728.19,"e":729.83,"en":"Just one more thing.","zh":"还有一件事。"},{"s":729.83,"e":732.99,"en":"I'll pay everything with my own card, right?","zh":"我会用自己的卡支付所有费用，对吗？"},{"s":732.99,"e":735.25,"en":"And I'll submit my claims form afterwards?","zh":"然后我再提交索赔表吗？"},{"s":735.25,"e":736.85,"en":"No problem.","zh":"没问题。"},{"s":736.85,"e":739.25,"en":"Just remember to keep all your receipts.","zh":"只要记住保留所有收据即可。"},{"s":739.25,"e":741.91,"en":"You remember the trouble you had last time.","zh":"你还记得上次遇到的麻烦。"},{"s":741.91,"e":1042.1,"en":"Oh, don't remind me.","zh":"哦，别提醒我。"}]},{"id":"2022-12-1-4","label":"篇章 2","questions":"第 19–21 题","start":1042.1,"end":1210.61,"sentences":[{"s":1043.94,"e":1054.45,"en":"Sunshine and high temperatures can mean picnics in parks and trips to beaches, but they can make your body react in some strange ways.","zh":"阳光和高温意味着可以在公园和海滩之旅，但他们可以让你的身体做出一些奇怪的反应。"},{"s":1054.45,"e":1058.9,"en":"First, sunshine can actually affect your breath.","zh":"首先，阳光实际上会影响你的呼吸。"},{"s":1058.9,"e":1074.62,"en":"You may think that summer is the perfect time to go on a date or chat with an attractive boy or girl, but excessive heat can cause you to lose water, which has been proven to have a pretty unattractive side effect, bad breath.","zh":"你可能认为夏天是完美的约会或聊天的时间和一个有吸引力的男孩或女孩，但过度高温会导致你失水，已被证明具有相当不吸引人的副作用，口臭。"},{"s":1074.62,"e":1078.74,"en":"When you are lacking water, your mouth becomes dry.","zh":"当你缺水时，你的嘴巴就会干燥。"},{"s":1078.74,"e":1084.44,"en":"Bacteria accumulates because there isn't enough water in your mouth to wash it away.","zh":"细菌积聚是因为体内水分不足用嘴巴漱口。"},{"s":1084.44,"e":1088.22,"en":"Sunshine can stop you from sweating too.","zh":"阳光也可以阻止你出汗。"},{"s":1088.22,"e":1100.46,"en":"The body's normal temperature is 36 to 37 degrees centigrade, but if it heats up to 40 to 41 degrees, you may find yourself getting heat stroke.","zh":"人体的正常体温是36至37摄氏度，但如果温度升至40到41度，你可能会发现自己中暑。"},{"s":1100.46,"e":1112.4,"en":"At that point, your heat regulatory system can essentially quit, which stops you from sweating, as your body tries to keep water around your vital organs.","zh":"此时，你的体温调节系统可以本质上就是戒烟，这样你就不会出汗了，因为你的身体会努力保持周围的水分重要器官。"},{"s":1112.4,"e":1118.52,"en":"However, the sun can have a positive influence on your body by raising your energy levels.","zh":"然而，阳光可以产生积极的影响通过提高你的能量水平来对你的身体产生影响。"},{"s":1118.52,"e":1124.52,"en":"You might feel like the sun is giving you extra energy for your day, which is actually happening.","zh":"你可能会觉得太阳正在给予为你的每一天补充能量，确实正在发生。"},{"s":1124.52,"e":1132.62,"en":"And vitamin D from sunshine can help your body to absorb certain minerals which are linked to building stronger bones.","zh":"阳光中的维生素D可以帮助你身体吸收某些矿物质，这些矿物质与从而强健骨骼。"},{"s":1132.62,"e":1210.61,"en":"Therefore, I suggest you spend more time in the park with your friends, but make sure you apply lots of skin protection and fill up those water bottles too.","zh":"因此，我建议你多花点时间和朋友一起去公园，但一定要你涂了很多皮肤保护剂并填充还有那些水瓶。"}]},{"id":"2022-12-1-5","label":"篇章 3","questions":"第 22–25 题","start":1210.61,"end":1411.45,"sentences":[{"s":1212.91,"e":1219.03,"en":"Left-handed people can find it inconvenient to do certain things, writing in a notebook, for example.","zh":"左撇子可能会觉得不方便做某些事情，写在笔记本上，例子。"},{"s":1219.03,"e":1223.79,"en":"But there are a number of advantages of being left-handed.","zh":"但有很多优点左撇子。"},{"s":1223.79,"e":1229.95,"en":"Research found that they were over-represented among fighters in combat sports.","zh":"研究发现，他们在格斗运动中的战士。"},{"s":1229.95,"e":1233.89,"en":"Left-handed fighters also had higher chances to win.","zh":"左撇子战士也有更高的机会赢。"},{"s":1233.89,"e":1237.03,"en":"This confirms the fighter theory.","zh":"这证实了战斗机理论。"},{"s":1237.03,"e":1240.93,"en":"Left-handers may also be better at remembering events.","zh":"左撇子可能记忆力更好事件。"},{"s":1240.93,"e":1247.15,"en":"The explanation is that the two brain spheres of left-handers are more strongly connected.","zh":"解释是，两个大脑球体左撇子之间的联系更为紧密。"},{"s":1247.15,"e":1252.01,"en":"Being left-handed might be a factor in mathematical ability.","zh":"左撇子可能是数学能力。"},{"s":1252.01,"e":1259.35,"en":"An Italian study found that for simple arithmetic, there was little difference between right and left-handed performance.","zh":"意大利的一项研究发现，对于简单的算术来说，左右之间几乎没有区别手表演。"},{"s":1259.35,"e":1264.33,"en":"But for more difficult problem solving, left-handers won out.","zh":"但对于更困难的问题解决，左撇子获胜了。"},{"s":1264.33,"e":1267.49,"en":"No one understands the reason for this.","zh":"没有人明白其中的原因。"},{"s":1267.49,"e":1270.28,"en":"Left-handed people may think differently.","zh":"左撇子的想法可能有所不同。"},{"s":1270.28,"e":1279.47,"en":"In one study, researchers showed the participants columns of abstract illustrations and asked them which ones they would prefer.","zh":"在一项研究中，研究人员向参与者展示了抽象插图，并问他们哪些他们更喜欢。"},{"s":1279.47,"e":1284.09,"en":"Left-handed people were more likely to prefer the images on the left.","zh":"左撇子更有可能喜欢左边的图像。"},{"s":1284.09,"e":1287.77,"en":"Right-handed people preferred the ones on the right.","zh":"惯用右手的人更喜欢正确的。"},{"s":1287.77,"e":1292.13,"en":"Both groups disliked stuff on their opposite side.","zh":"两个群体都不喜欢对方的东西。"},{"s":1292.13,"e":1297.23,"en":"Left-handers are also over-represented in professional, interactive sports.","zh":"左撇子在职业中也占了很大比例，互动体育。"},{"s":1297.23,"e":1303.41,"en":"Researchers have looked at the influence of being left-handed on performance in interactive sports.","zh":"研究人员研究了左撇子在互动运动中的表现。"},{"s":1303.41,"e":1308.99,"en":"Those that require the fastest reaction give left-handers the biggest advantage.","zh":"那些需要最快反应的人会选择左边手最大的优势。"},{"s":1308.99,"e":1316.29,"en":"So, if you have a left-handed child, you should encourage them to play table tennis, baseball, and tennis.","zh":"所以如果你有一个左撇子孩子，你应该鼓励他们打乒乓球，棒球和网球。"},{"s":1316.29,"e":1411.45,"en":"Being left-handed maximizes their chances of success in these sports.","zh":"左撇子可以最大程度地提高成功的机会在这些运动中。"}]}]}];
